{"ref":"BDB, מַטְעָם","hw":"מַטְעָם","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">מַטְעָם</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> only pl. <strong>tasty</strong> or <strong>savoury food, dainties</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">מַטְעַמִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:4\" href=\"/Genesis.27.4\">Gn 27:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:7\" href=\"/Genesis.27.7\">7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:9\" href=\"/Genesis.27.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:14\" href=\"/Genesis.27.14\">14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:17\" href=\"/Genesis.27.17\">17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:31\" href=\"/Genesis.27.31\">31</a> (all J); sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַטְעַמּוֹתָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.3\">Pr 23:3</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מַטְעַמֹּתָיו</span> v <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:6\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.6\">6</a>.","next":"BDB, טָעַן","prev":"BDB, טַ֫עַם"}